# JSONPlaceholder
// A server for practice:  someone's todos to tick, add and remove, and posts with their comments.
// Every thing it shows is in JSONPlaceholder.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it;  each type below adds to its type there,
// with `<extend>`, so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.
// It answers each change as if it saved it, and keeps nothing:  what you add here is gone when it's asked again.

a "jsonplaceholder page" is a thing:
	"new todo" is a new todo with user id = 1
	// Whose todos and posts these are:  the first person it has
	its "person" is the jsonplaceholder user whose id is 1
	// Theirs, from every todo
	its "todos" is every todo where its user id is 1

	to add the new todo:
		add its new todo to the saved todos
		set its new todo to a new todo with user id = 1

	to draw it:
		<stack spacing="xl">
			<stack spacing="sm">
				<header size="large">Practice, on JSONPlaceholder</header>
				<text color="grey">Tick a todo, add one, remove one:  each goes to the server, which answers as if it saved it, and keeps nothing.</text>
			</stack>
			<stack spacing="sm">
				<header size="medium">Their todos</header>
				{draw the checklist of it}
			</stack>
			<stack spacing="sm">
				<header size="medium">What they wrote</header>
				{draw the post list of it}
			</stack>
			<text size="small" paragraph>
				From <link link="https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com">JSONPlaceholder</link>, asked for as you look.
			</text>
		</stack>

	to draw its checklist:
		<stack spacing="sm">
			<form value={its new todo}>
				<input name="title" placeholder="Water the plants" aria-label="Something to do" fluid action>
					<button slot="action" color="primary" disabled={its new todo's title is ""} onClick={add the new todo}>Add</button>
				</input>
			</form>
			{draw the todo list of it}
		</stack>

	to draw its todo list:
		for todo in its todos
		while waiting: <loader visible inline text>{"Asking JSONPlaceholder"}</loader>
		if that fails say "JSONPlaceholder can't be reached just now."

	to draw its post list:
		for post in its person's posts
		while waiting: <loader visible inline text>{"Asking JSONPlaceholder"}</loader>
		if that fails say "JSONPlaceholder can't be reached just now."

# A todo
// Ticked as it's done;  each tick, and each removal, goes to the server at once.

a todo:
	to draw it:
		<form value={it}>
			<stack direction="horizontal" align="center" justify="between" spacing="sm">
				<ui-checkbox name="completed" label={its title} />
				<button icon="close" size="mini" appearance="transparent" aria-label="Remove" title="Remove" onClick={remove it from the saved todos}/>
			</stack>
		</form>

# A post
// Its title, what it says, and its comments:  read from the post's own address, the first time it's drawn.

a post:
	to draw it:
		<header size="small">{its title}</header>
		<text>{its body}</text>
		for comment in its comments
		while waiting: <loader visible inline text>{"Asking for its comments"}</loader>

// Each comment, as Spell UI draws one:  named in full, `<ui-comment>`.

a comment:
	to draw it:
		<ui-comment>
			<content>
				<author>{its email}</author>
				<description>{its body}</description>
			</content>
		</ui-comment>
